#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:70
msgid ""
"Odoo uses two rules to compute the price of a product when a rental order is "
"created:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:72
msgid "Only one price line is used."
msgstr "Endast en prisrad används."

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:73
msgid "The cheapest line is selected."
msgstr "Den billigaste linjen väljs."

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:76
msgid ""
"A bike rental company offers the following rental prices for its electric "
"bikes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:78
msgid "1 day: $100"
msgstr "1 dag: $100"

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:79
msgid "3 days: $250"
msgstr "3 dagar: 250 USD"

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:80
msgid "1 week: $500"
msgstr "1 vecka: $500"

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:82
msgid ""
"A customer wants to rent this product for eight days. What price will they "
"pay?"
msgstr ""
"En kund vill hyra denna produkt i åtta dagar. Vilket pris kommer de att "
"betala?"

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:84
msgid ""
"After the order is created, Odoo chooses the second line because it is the "
"lowest price. The customer pays three times the '3 days' rate to cover eight "
"days, totaling $750."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:87
msgid ""
"1~\\text{day} * 8 &= 8~\\text{days} \\\\\n"
"3~\\text{days} + 3~\\text{days} + 3~\\text{days} &= 9~\\text{days} \\\\\n"
"1~\\text{week} + 1~\\text{week} &= 14~\\text{days} \\\\\n"
"\\\\\n"
"100 * 8 &= $800 \\\\\n"
"250 + 250 + 250 &= $750 \\\\\n"
"500 + 500 &= $1000\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:96
msgid "Therefore, the customer pays $750 for the eight-day rental period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:101
msgid "Rental pricelist rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:103
msgid ""
"Extra rental prices are configured in the product's :guilabel:`Prices` tab. "
"The prices are configured like advanced :doc:`pricelists <sales/"
"products_prices/prices/pricing>`, where the following fields work as "
"conditions for the price to be applied:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:107
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Pricelist`: The pricelist for which the pricelist rule is valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:108
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Min Quantity`: To trigger the Pricelist rule, the quantity must "
"meet or exceed the minimum quantity value. The unit of measure follows the "
"product's :guilabel:`Periodicity` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:110
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Validity`: The starting date or date range when the pricelist "
"rule is active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:111
msgid ":guilabel:`Company`: The company for which the pricelist rule is valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:114
msgid "How Minimum Quantity is computed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:116
msgid ""
"Configuring discounted prices based on rental duration requires price rules "
"with a :guilabel:`Min. Quantity`. The :guilabel:`Min. Quantity` field is "
"computed differently for the **Rental** app than for the **Sales** and "
"**Subscription** apps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:120
msgid ""
"The :guilabel:`Min. Quantity` is computed based on the rental duration and "
"the quantity on the sales order line (SOL). The unit of time for "
"the :guilabel:`Min. Quantity` field is based on the "
"product's :guilabel:`Periodicity` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:124
msgid "The formula used is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/rental.rst:126
msgid ""
"\\text{Min. Quantity} = \\text{Quantity on SOL}*\\text{Rental duration}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

