#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:3
msgid "Margins"
msgstr "Marginaler"

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:5
msgid ""
"A *sales margin* is the profit gained from the sale of a product or service "
"after all the costs related to it have been accounted for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:11
msgid ""
"To activate the *Margins* feature, go to the :menuselection:`Sales app --> "
"Configuration --> Settings`. In the :guilabel:`Pricing` section, enable "
"the :guilabel:`Margins` checkbox. Then click :guilabel:`Save`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:18
msgid "Configure price and cost"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:20
msgid ""
"Each individual product must be configured to automatically calculate the "
"sales margin on each quotation and :abbr:`SO (sales order)` line. To enable "
"this feature, navigate to :menuselection:`Sales app --> Products --> "
"Products`. Click :guilabel:`New` and on the product form fill out "
"the :guilabel:`Sales Price` and :guilabel:`Cost` fields in the *General "
"Information* tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:None
msgid "Sales Price and Cost fields of a product form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:28
msgid "Odoo calculates the margin with the following formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:30
msgid ""
"Sales~Margin = Sales~Price - Cost\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:33
msgid "The margin percentage is calculated with the following formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:35
msgid ""
"\\frac{Sales~Price - Cost~Price}{Sales~Price} \\times 100\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:39
msgid "Compute margins on sales orders"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:41
msgid ""
"To calculate the margins on a :abbr:`SO (sales order)`, navigate "
"to :menuselection:`Sales app --> Orders --> Quotations` and :ref:`create a "
"new quotation <sales/create_quotations/create-quotation>`. While adding "
"products to the quotation, a new field, :guilabel:`Margin`, automatically "
"appears at the bottom of the to the quotation. This field displays the "
"order's total margin in the configured currency as well as the percentage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:None
msgid "Sales order with Margin field on the bottom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:53
msgid "Compute margins on sales order lines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:55
msgid ""
"To display a product's margin and the margin percentage per line item, click "
"the :icon:`oi-settings-adjust` :guilabel:`(settings adjust)` icon in "
"the :guilabel:`Order Lines` tab. Then, select the checkboxes "
"for :guilabel:`Margin` and :guilabel:`Margin (%)`. The :guilabel:`Margin` "
"and :guilabel:`Margin (%)` columns are not displayed by default, but once "
"enabled, the columns appear on all new and existing quotations "
"and :abbr:`SOs (sales orders)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:61
msgid ""
"The :guilabel:`Margin` column shows the profit earned from the sale after "
"accounting for all associated costs, in the configured currency value. "
"The :guilabel:`Margin (%)` shows the margin value as a percentage. The "
"margin for one unit is multiplied by the quantity to determine the margin "
"for the entire line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:66
msgid ""
"Editing the :guilabel:`Margin` column automatically recalculates "
"the :guilabel:`Unit Price` of the product on the :abbr:`SO (sales order)`. "
"Both columns can be edited on the :abbr:`SO (sales order)` until an invoice "
"is created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:71
msgid ""
"The :guilabel:`Margin` and :guilabel:`Margin (%)` columns are not editable "
"since they are automatic calculations. To change the calculation, refer "
"to :ref:`Configure price and cost <sales/margin/configure-price-and-cost>` "
"section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:76
msgid "Margin calculation with a pricelist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:78
msgid ""
"To calculate the margin with an applied pricelist, begin with configuring a "
"pricelist for the product. Follow these steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:81
msgid ""
"Go to :menuselection:`Sales app --> Products --> Pricelists` and click "
"the :guilabel:`New` button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:83
msgid ""
"Enter the name of the pricelist and click :guilabel:`Add a line` "
"to :ref:`create a new pricelist rule <sales/products/price-rules>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:85
msgid "Configure the pricelist and click :guilabel:`Save & Close` button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:86
msgid ""
"Go to :menuselection:`Sales app --> Orders --> Quotations` and :ref:`create "
"a quotation <sales/create_quotations/create-quotation>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:88
msgid "In the :guilabel:`Pricelist` field, select the newly made pricelist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:89
msgid ""
"Click on :guilabel:`Update Prices` to refresh the product price and margin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:92
msgid "Use case: Conditional discounts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:94
msgid ""
"A clothing store wants to create a seasonal 5% discount on blue denim jeans. "
"The discount requires a minimum of two pairs of jeans in an order and is "
"valid only from October to the end of December."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:97
msgid ""
"First go to :menuselection:`Sales app --> Products --> Pricelists` and "
"create a new pricelist for the seasonal discount. Click :guilabel:`Add a "
"line` to configure a price rule for seasonal discount. Include the specific "
"product it applies to, the type of discount, the minimum quantity needed to "
"trigger the discount, and the date range the discount is active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:None
msgid "Pricelist Rules pop-up window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:105
msgid ""
"After saving the pricelist, go to a :abbr:`SO (sales order)` containing blue "
"denim jeans and select the newly created pricelist in "
"the :guilabel:`Pricelist` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:None
msgid "Sales order with a new pricelist selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:112
msgid ""
"The discount only applies if the :abbr:`SO (sales order)` meets both the "
"date range and minimum quantity requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/sales/sales/sales_quotations/margin.rst:115
msgid ""
"After the changes are made, click :icon:`fa-refresh` :guilabel:`Update "
